  t["Supongamos lo contrario: que $\\sqrt{2} = \\frac{a}{b}$ con $a$ y $b$ enteros, y que la fracción ya está <strong>simplificada</strong> (si no lo estuviera, se simplifica antes). Ese detalle será el que estalle al final."] = "Suppose the opposite: that $\\sqrt{2} = \\frac{a}{b}$ with $a$ and $b$ integers, and that the fraction is already <strong>in lowest terms</strong> (if it were not, you would reduce it first). That detail is the one that blows up at the end.";
  t["Supongamos que se pudiera hacer una lista con <em>todos</em> los reales entre 0 y 1."] = "Suppose a list could be made of <em>all</em> the reals between 0 and 1.";
  t["Suponiendo que las inversas que hagan falta existen, despeja $X$ en $"] = "Assuming that any inverses needed exist, isolate $X$ in $";
